// Vault, comprehensively: servirtium-vcr's pre-recorded/from-testcontainers
// "Pattern for comprehensive suites" (README) applied to HashiCorp Vault
// 1.13.0 (MPL-2.0, the last release before the BSL), after the CouchDB pilot.
//
// Two describe blocks, two sets of tapes:
//
// 1. "modules/vault": ported from testcontainers-go modules/vault/vault_test.go
//    (by way of testcontainers-ae). It tests the MODULE: the root token the
//    token() option chooses, the init commands, the defaults. Its two tapes
//    (reads_and_writes_secrets_with_the_chosen_token, runs_with_no_options)
//    are the original representative ones.
//
// 2. "Vault HTTP API": written for servirtium-vcr. Re-usable recordings of
//    Vault's HTTP API, one tape per scenario, for any language's tests to
//    replay with no Vault. This is the comprehensive part. Component-level
//    tests of Vault's API, never "end-to-end": the tapes stand in for Vault.
//
// PORTING: this file is the reference for what each tape holds; the tapes are
// the re-usable part. A port is a test in your language and test framework
// that makes the same requests in the same order against a Servirtium replay
// server loaded with the tape, and checks the same things. Every request is
// plain HTTP/1.1 with these headers and no others:
//   User-Agent: testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)
//   Content-Type: application/json   (only when there is a body; the one
//                                     PATCH uses application/merge-patch+json)
//   X-Vault-Token: ...               (every case but the ones that show
//                                     "no token", see below)
//   X-Vault-Wrap-TTL: 60             (one request, wraps_a_response_...)
// Playback is strict about method, path (query string included, as written
// here), the recorded request headers and the body (byte for byte: send the
// JSON bodies exactly as written in this file, no spaces), and fails a case
// whose recorded requests are not all made. Host, Connection and
// Content-Length are on the tapes but are transport headers, not compared.
// Vault's "list" operation is the LIST verb or GET with ?list=true; these
// tapes use GET ?list=true, which any HTTP client can send.
//
// Login, and "already logged in"
// ------------------------------
// Vault's session credential is a token (X-Vault-Token). Logging in gets its
// own tapes: logs_in_with_userpass_and_ends_the_session (a wrong and the
// right password, who-am-I, renew, revoke) and logs_in_with_an_approle
// (enable the method, make a role and a secret id, log in with a wrong and
// the right secret id). Every other case is ALREADY LOGGED IN: its requests
// carry the client token that the userpass login of user "alice" mints, and
// the login is not on that case's tape. When recording, the test sets Vault
// up once through the dev-mode root token (userpass enabled, policies
// tcae-admin and tcae-reader, users alice and bob), then logs alice in
// directly against the container, outside the recorder (login_live below),
// so the token is real. None of that is recorded, and the root token never
// appears on a tape. The case enforces_a_read_only_policy also logs bob (a
// reader) in; the cases that show "no token" send none.
//
// PORTING, getting into the logged-in state without the login tapes: send
// any `X-Vault-Token: <anything>` header on every request. The tapes hold the
// token as X_VAULT_TOKEN_N (Servirtium's redact_credential_header preset) and
// playback matches a credential header on PRESENCE, not value. A consequence:
// a replay cannot tell a good token from a forged one, so the cases that show
// a refusal for a missing token send no header at all, and the case that
// shows a wrong token (refuses_a_client_without_a_valid_token) records Vault's
// 403 for it but replays against any header. Passwords in a login body are
// labelled literal redactions (REDACTED[alice], REDACTED[alice-wrong-password]),
// put back on replay, so the right and the wrong password stay distinct: a
// port sends the real test passwords "alice-pass" and "not-the-password".
//
// What varies between runs, and what the tapes do with it
// --------------------------------------------------------
// Every rule is registered in api_rules() below with its reason; the
// "## [Recording rules]" table at the end of each tape lists them and the
// interactions each touched. In short:
//   - normalized ({{name-N}}, the same token wherever the value recurs,
//     because a client sends it back): client tokens (a token used as a
//     header is X_VAULT_TOKEN_N wherever it appears; one that is only sent in
//     a body, or never sent, is {{token-N}}), token accessors ({{accessor-N}}),
//     mount accessors ({{mount-accessor-N}}), uuids ({{uuid-N}}: entity ids,
//     mount uuids, approle role ids and secret ids), and transit
//     ciphertexts, signatures and HMACs ({{blob-N}}: "vault:v1:..." differs on
//     every run).
//   - collapsed (one constant; nobody sends them back): request_id, times
//     (RFC 3339 and Unix), the cluster's name, a token's remaining ttl.
//   - redacted: the token header and the login passwords.
//   - left out: Date.
// PORTING: in playback a normalized or redacted value comes back as its
// token, verbatim ("{{token-1}}"); treat every token, accessor, uuid and blob
// as an opaque string (never assert its length or shape) and send it back
// exactly as received. Send the braces as they are: playback compares paths
// and bodies byte for byte, so a client that percent-encodes `{` will not
// match. Deterministic values are left alone: versions, key names, policy text.
//
// Awkward points (random order, and the workaround)
// -------------------------------------------------
// Vault 1.13 copies the data of GET sys/mounts, sys/auth, sys/mounts/<path>,
// sys/auth/<path> and .../tune to the TOP LEVEL of the response as well (a
// legacy form), and that copy's keys come in a different order on every
// request, so a tape of it would never be stable. These cases use
// sys/internal/ui/mounts[/<path>] instead, which gives the same mount facts
// (type, accessor, options, config) with no legacy copy, so with sorted keys.
// An opt-in "stable key order" option in Servirtium's core would let a case
// read sys/mounts directly. Every other response here is already stable.
//
// In and out of scope
// -------------------
// In: health, seal status, leader and init (public, no token); mounts and
// auth methods (enable, read, tune, disable); ACL policies (write, read, list,
// delete, capabilities) and their enforcement; the KV v2 engine (write, read,
// CAS, versions, metadata, soft delete, undelete, destroy, list, patch,
// max_versions pruning) and KV v1; the transit engine (key create, read,
// config, rotate, list, delete; encrypt, decrypt, rewrap; sign and verify,
// hash, HMAC); tokens (create, lookup, lookup by accessor, renew, revoke,
// revoke by accessor, use limits, parents and children); response wrapping
// and the cubbyhole; the representative errors 400, 403, 404, 405.
// Out: seal, unseal and init (a dev server is unsealed and initialized, and
// sealing it would end the suite); HA, standbys, replication and raft (health
// is always 200, never 429/473/503); other secrets engines (database, PKI,
// SSH, AWS, TOTP: they need an external system, or generate random key
// material no client could replay), identity/OIDC, namespaces and other
// enterprise features, audit devices and telemetry (node specific), leases of
// dynamic secrets, and anything streaming. Each could be a later case.
//
// Running it (from pre-recorded/from-testcontainers):
//   ae test vault/test_vault.ae                         container, no Servirtium
//   TCAE_VCR=record   ae test vault/test_vault.ae       write the tapes
//   TCAE_VCR=check    ae test vault/test_vault.ae       fail if a tape changed
//   TCAE_VCR=playback ae test vault/test_vault.ae       no container: the tapes
// The API cases share one container (started on the first one and removed at
// the end); the module cases each start their own.

import std.spec
import std.string
import std.http.client
import std.json
import testcontainers as tc
import testcontainers.docker
import testcontainers.testing
import servirtium
import modules.vault

const IMAGE = "hashicorp/vault:1.13.0"
const TOKEN = "root-token"

// The User-Agent this test's HTTP client sends, as an app's client library
// would: Go's net/http adds `Go-http-client/1.1` by itself, Aether's
// std.http.client adds none. Set here, in the test's own client, so the
// recordings show a representative request; Servirtium records what the
// client sends and adds nothing of its own.
const USER_AGENT = "testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)"

// The token the logged-in cases send in playback, where there is no Vault to
// log in to. Any value does: the tapes match X-Vault-Token on presence.
const PLAYBACK_TOKEN = "any-value-replay-matches-on-presence"

// The passwords of the two users the live setup makes (test values for a
// throwaway container).
const ALICE_PASSWORD = "alice-pass"
const BOB_PASSWORD = "bob-pass"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// HTTP helpers
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// One HTTP request: (status, body, error). hdrs are "Name: value" lines;
// ctype is the body's Content-Type (none when the body is empty); tok "" sends
// no X-Vault-Token.
fn http_send(method: string, url: string, tok: string, hdrs: string[], ctype: string, body: string) -> (int, string, string) {
    req = client.request(method, url)
    client.set_header(req, "User-Agent", USER_AGENT)
    client.set_timeout(req, 30s)
    if string.length(tok) > 0 { client.set_header(req, "X-Vault-Token", tok) }
    for h in hdrs {
        colon = string.index_of(h, ":")
        client.set_header(req, string.substring(h, 0, colon), string.trim(string.substring(h, colon + 1, string.length(h))))
    }
    if string.length(body) > 0 { client.set_body(req, string.bytes(body), ctype) }
    r, err = client.send_request(req)
    client.request_free(req)
    if err != "" { return 0, "", err }
    st = client.response_status(r)
    b = client.response_body(r)
    client.response_free(r)
    return st, b, ""
}

// (status, body, error); token "" sends no X-Vault-Token. Used by the module
// cases.
fn call_api(method: string, url: string, tok: string, body: string) -> (int, string, string) {
    return http_send(method, url, tok, [], "application/json", body)
}

// data.data.<key> of a KV-v2 read response.
fn kv_field(body: string, key: string) -> string {
    doc, perr = json.parse(body)
    if perr != "" { return "" }
    d1, _ = json.object_get(doc, "data")
    d2, _ = json.object_get(d1, "data")
    v, _ = json.object_get(d2, key)
    s, _ = json.get_string(v)
    json.free(doc)
    return s
}

// A string in a JSON body by a dotted path ("auth.client_token",
// "data.keys.0"); "" when absent or not a string.
fn jstr(body: string, path: string) -> string {
    doc, err = json.parse(body)
    if err != "" { return "" }
    let v: ptr = doc
    rest = path
    while string.length(rest) > 0 && v != null {
        p = rest
        dot = string.index_of(rest, ".")
        if dot >= 0 {
            p = string.substring(rest, 0, dot)
            rest = string.substring(rest, dot + 1, string.length(rest))
        } else {
            rest = ""
        }
        if json.json_type(v) == json.JSON_ARRAY {
            idx, _ = string.to_int(p)
            a, _ = json.array_get(v, idx)
            v = a
        } else {
            o, _ = json.object_get(v, p)
            v = o
        }
    }
    out = ""
    if v != null {
        s, serr = json.get_string(v)
        if serr == "" { out = string.copy(s) }
    }
    json.free(doc)
    return out
}

// HCL for a policy, as the JSON string Vault takes: write ' for the double
// quotes HCL needs and this puts \" there, so the test source stays readable.
fn hcl(s: string) -> string {
    return string.replace_all(string.replace_all(s, "\n", "\\n"), "'", "\\\"")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The API cases: the base URL, the logged-in token, and requests
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

var api: string = ""
var tok: string = ""

// A logged-in request with a JSON body (or none): (status, body). A transport
// error fails the case.
fn vault_(method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    return vault_as(tok, method, path, body)
}

// The same with the given token ("" sends none).
fn vault_as(t: string, method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send(method, "${api}/v1/${path}", t, [], "application/json", body)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// With a Content-Type of its own and extra "Name: value" headers.
fn vault_with(t: string, method: string, path: string, ctype: string, hdrs: string[], body: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send(method, "${api}/v1/${path}", t, hdrs, ctype, body)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// A request with no token at all.
fn anonymous(method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    return vault_as("", method, path, body)
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The live container the API cases share (record, check and off modes only)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

var shared_addr: string = ""
var shared_container: ptr = null

// Set Vault up through the root token, once per container (not recorded):
// userpass, two policies and two users. tcae-admin may do anything, so every
// logged-in case can; tcae-reader may only read and list under tcae/.
fn setup_live(addr: string) -> int {
    admin = "path '*' { capabilities = ['create','read','update','delete','list','sudo','patch'] }"
    reader = "path 'secret/data/tcae/*' { capabilities = ['read'] }\npath 'secret/metadata/tcae/*' { capabilities = ['read','list'] }"
    steps = [
        "POST|sys/auth/userpass|{\"type\":\"userpass\"}",
        "PUT|sys/policies/acl/tcae-admin|{\"policy\":\"${hcl(admin)}\"}",
        "PUT|sys/policies/acl/tcae-reader|{\"policy\":\"${hcl(reader)}\"}",
        "POST|auth/userpass/users/alice|{\"password\":\"${ALICE_PASSWORD}\",\"policies\":\"tcae-admin\"}",
        "POST|auth/userpass/users/bob|{\"password\":\"${BOB_PASSWORD}\",\"policies\":\"tcae-reader\"}"
    ]
    for step in steps {
        p1 = string.index_of(step, "|")
        m = string.substring(step, 0, p1)
        rest = string.substring(step, p1 + 1, string.length(step))
        p2 = string.index_of(rest, "|")
        path = string.substring(rest, 0, p2)
        body = string.substring(rest, p2 + 1, string.length(rest))
        st, b, err = http_send(m, "${addr}/v1/${path}", TOKEN, [], "application/json", body)
        spec.assert_ok(err, "setup ${path}")
        spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "setup ${path}: ${b}")
        if st != 204 { return 0 }
    }
    return 1
}

// The shared container's base URL, starting it (and setting it up) on first
// use ("" on failure).
fn shared() -> string {
    if string.length(shared_addr) > 0 { return shared_addr }
    c, err = vault.run(IMAGE) { token(TOKEN) }
    spec.assert_ok(err, "vault starts")
    if err != "" { return "" }
    shared_container = c as ptr
    a, aerr = vault.http_host_address(c)
    spec.assert_ok(aerr, "http host address")
    if aerr != "" { return "" }
    if setup_live(a) == 0 { return "" }
    shared_addr = a
    return shared_addr
}

// Log a user in directly against the container, outside any recording: the
// client token a logged-in case carries.
fn login_live(addr: string, user: string, password: string) -> string {
    st, b, err = http_send("POST", "${addr}/v1/auth/userpass/login/${user}", "", [], "application/json", "{\"password\":\"${password}\"}")
    spec.assert_ok(err, "log ${user} in (not recorded)")
    spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "log ${user} in (not recorded): ${b}")
    return jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
}

var bob_tok: string = ""

// Start a logged-in API case: in a live mode, the shared container, a fresh
// token for alice (and for bob when asked) and, should an earlier failed run
// have left them, the case's mounts, auth methods, policies and secrets
// removed (cleanup lists "path" strings to DELETE; none of it is recorded);
// then the recording. Sets `api`, `tok` and `bob_tok`; returns the recording
// handle, and ok = 0 when the case cannot run.
fn begin(case_: string, cleanup: string[], with_bob: int) -> (ptr, int) {
    addr = ""
    tok = PLAYBACK_TOKEN
    bob_tok = PLAYBACK_TOKEN
    if servirtium.live() == 1 {
        addr = shared()
        if addr == "" { return null, 0 }
        tok = login_live(addr, "alice", ALICE_PASSWORD)
        if with_bob == 1 { bob_tok = login_live(addr, "bob", BOB_PASSWORD) }
        for p in cleanup { http_send("DELETE", "${addr}/v1/${p}", tok, [], "application/json", "") }
    }
    base, rec = servirtium.recording("vault", case_, addr)
    api = base
    return rec, 1
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Recording rules
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// The module cases' rules.
fn module_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // Servirtium's credential preset: the token is written as
    // X_VAULT_TOKEN_1, and playback matches X-Vault-Token on presence, so it
    // needs no secret.
    servirtium.redact_credential_header("X-Vault-Token")
    // What differs run to run: request and cluster ids, the cluster's name,
    // created_time, and the Unix times of server_time_utc and the transit
    // key's versions.
    servirtium.normalize(servirtium.UUID, "uuid")
    servirtium.collapse("vault-cluster-[0-9a-f]+", "vault-cluster-0")
    servirtium.collapse(servirtium.RFC3339, "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z")
    servirtium.collapse(servirtium.EPOCH_TIMESTAMP, "946684800")
}

// The API cases' rules. Rules apply to every recording after them, so the two
// blocks each clear and register their own.
fn api_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // The session credential. Registered FIRST: the preset writes each
    // distinct token as X_VAULT_TOKEN_N in the header and, because a token
    // is 8+ characters, wherever else the same value appears (a login's
    // client_token, a lookup's id, a body that names it). Later rules only
    // see the rest.
    servirtium.redact_credential_header("X-Vault-Token")
    // The passwords in the login bodies: labelled literal redactions, not a
    // collapse, so playback puts the real text back before comparing and
    // still tells the right password from the wrong one.
    servirtium.redact(servirtium.FIELD_REQUEST_BODY, "\"password\":\"${ALICE_PASSWORD}\"", "\"password\":\"REDACTED[alice]\"")
    servirtium.redact(servirtium.FIELD_REQUEST_BODY, "\"password\":\"not-the-password\"", "\"password\":\"REDACTED[alice-wrong-password]\"")
    // A token that is never used as a header (a child token only looked up
    // by body, a wrapping token the client puts in a header is already
    // covered above): "hvs." and a long base64url string, normalized since a
    // client sends it back in a body.
    servirtium.normalize("hvs\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}", "token")
    // A request id on every body: nobody sends it back.
    servirtium.collapse("(?<=\"request_id\":\")[0-9a-f-]{36}(?=\")", "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000")
    // Every other uuid: entity ids, mount uuids, the cluster id, approle role
    // and secret ids (a client sends the last two back in the login body).
    servirtium.normalize(servirtium.UUID, "uuid")
    // A token's accessor (24 characters; a client may send it back to look a
    // token up or revoke it), and a mount's ("kv_" or "auth_userpass_" and
    // 8 hex digits; read back by whoever lists mounts, never sent).
    servirtium.normalize("(?<=\"accessor\":\"|\"wrapped_accessor\":\")[A-Za-z0-9]{24}(?=\")", "accessor")
    servirtium.normalize("(?<=\"accessor\":\")[a-z_]+_[0-9a-f]{8}(?=\")", "mount-accessor")
    // Transit's ciphertext, signature and HMAC: "vault:v<N>:<base64>". The
    // ciphertext carries a random nonce, the keys are random, so every run
    // differs; a client sends a ciphertext back (decrypt, rewrap) and a
    // signature back (verify), hence normalized. (The key version is lost
    // with the value; the response's "key_version" says it.)
    servirtium.normalize("vault:v[0-9]+:[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+", "blob")
    // The cluster's name, a random suffix.
    servirtium.collapse("vault-cluster-[0-9a-f]+", "vault-cluster-0")
    // Times: RFC 3339 with nanoseconds (created_time, deletion_time,
    // issue_time, expire_time, a wrapping token's creation_time). Not the Go
    // zero time "0001-01-01T00:00:00Z" (/sys/leader's active_time, meaning
    // never), which is stable and means something.
    servirtium.collapse(string.concat("(?!0001-)", servirtium.RFC3339), "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z")
    // Unix times, by field: the server clock, a token's creation, a transit
    // key version's creation ("keys":{"1":1794074791}).
    servirtium.collapse("(?<=\"server_time_utc\":|\"creation_time\":)1[0-9]{9}", "946684800")
    servirtium.collapse("(?<=\"[0-9]\":)1[0-9]{9}", "946684800")
    // A token's remaining ttl, counting down in seconds from the 1 hour the
    // cases ask for (or from the 32 days a login gets): 3599 one moment and
    // 3598 the next. Collapsed to the full hour; a wrapping token's
    // ttl 60 and a root-like 0 are not matched.
    servirtium.collapse("(?<=\"ttl\":)(?:35[0-9]{2}|3600|276[0-9]{4})(?=[,}])", "3600")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

main() {
    fw = spec.init()
    if servirtium.skip_if_no_engine(fw) == 1 { return spec.run_summary(fw) }

    module_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "modules/vault") {
        spec.after_each() callback { testing.cleanup_all() }

        spec.it("reads and writes secrets with the chosen token (TestVault)") callback {
            addr = ""
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                c, err = vault.run(IMAGE) {
                    token(TOKEN)
                    init_command(["secrets enable transit", "write -f transit/keys/my-key"])
                    init_command(["kv put secret/test1 foo1=bar1"])
                }
                testing.cleanup_container(c)
                spec.assert_ok(err, "vault starts and the init commands succeed")
                if err != "" { return }
                a, aerr = vault.http_host_address(c)
                spec.assert_ok(aerr, "http host address")
                spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(a, "http://localhost:") == 1, "an http:// URL: ${a}")
                addr = a

                // Get secret path / From vault CLI
                code, out, eerr = tc.exec(c, ["vault", "kv", "get", "-format=json", "secret/test1"])
                spec.assert_ok(eerr, "exec vault kv get")
                spec.assert_eq(code, 0, "vault kv get exits 0")
                spec.assert_str_eq(kv_field(out, "foo1"), "bar1", "the CLI reads what the init command wrote")
            }
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("vault", "reads_and_writes_secrets_with_the_chosen_token", addr)

            hs, hb, herr = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/sys/health", "", "")
            spec.assert_ok(herr, "GET /v1/sys/health")
            spec.assert_eq(hs, 200, "health is 200 (initialized, unsealed, active)")
            spec.assert_contains(hb, "\"initialized\":true", "initialized")

            // Get secret path / From HTTP request (KV-v2)
            st, body, rerr = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/secret/data/test1", TOKEN, "")
            spec.assert_ok(rerr, "KV-v2 read")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "KV-v2 read is 200")
            spec.assert_str_eq(kv_field(body, "foo1"), "bar1", "the HTTP API reads the same secret")

            // The transit key made by the first init command
            tk, _, terr = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/transit/keys/my-key", TOKEN, "")
            spec.assert_ok(terr, "transit key read")
            spec.assert_eq(tk, 200, "the transit key exists")

            // Write secret / From KV-v2 HTTP request
            ws, _, werr = call_api("POST", "${base}/v1/secret/data/test3", TOKEN, "{\"data\":{\"foo\":\"bar\"}}")
            spec.assert_ok(werr, "KV-v2 write")
            spec.assert_eq(ws, 200, "KV-v2 write is 200")
            _, wb, _ = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/secret/data/test3", TOKEN, "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(kv_field(wb, "foo"), "bar", "the written secret reads back")

            // The token is really required, and only the chosen one works
            no, _, _ = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/secret/data/test1", "", "")
            spec.assert_eq(no, 403, "no token: refused")
            wrong, _, _ = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/secret/data/test1", "not-the-token", "")
            spec.assert_eq(wrong, 403, "wrong token: refused")

            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        spec.it("runs with no options (dev-mode defaults)") callback {
            addr = ""
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                c, err = vault.run(IMAGE)
                testing.cleanup_container(c)
                spec.assert_ok(err, "vault starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                a, _ = vault.http_host_address(c)
                addr = a
                code, out, _ = tc.exec(c, ["sh", "-c", "echo $VAULT_ADDR"])
                spec.assert_eq(code, 0, "exec")
                spec.assert_str_eq(string.trim(out), "http://0.0.0.0:8200", "the module's VAULT_ADDR")
            }
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("vault", "runs_with_no_options", addr)
            hs, _, herr = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/sys/health", "", "")
            spec.assert_ok(herr, "health")
            spec.assert_eq(hs, 200, "health is 200")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        spec.it_when(servirtium.live(), "fails the run when an init command fails", "no container in playback") callback {
            c, err = vault.run(IMAGE) {
                token(TOKEN)
                tc.wait_deadline(20s)
                init_command(["kv put nosuch-mount/x a=b"])
            }
            testing.cleanup_container(c)
            spec.assert_true(err != "", "the failing init command is an error")
            spec.assert_contains(err, "run vault:", "wrapped like Go's")
        }
    }

    api_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "Vault HTTP API") {
        spec.after_each() callback { api = "" }

        // ---- the login tapes -----------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: the tape with the userpass login on it. No token on the
        // first requests.
        //   GET  /v1/auth/token/lookup-self                      -> 403 {"errors":["permission denied"]}
        //   POST /v1/auth/userpass/login/alice {"password":<wrong>} -> 500 (sic: Vault 1.13's status
        //        for bad credentials, not 400 or 401) {"errors":["invalid username or password"]}
        //   POST /v1/auth/userpass/login/alice {"password":<right>} -> 200,
        //        auth.client_token (X_VAULT_TOKEN_1), auth.policies ["default","tcae-admin"],
        //        auth.lease_duration 2764800, auth.renewable true
        //   GET  /v1/auth/token/lookup-self  X-Vault-Token: <client_token> -> 200,
        //        data.display_name "userpass-alice", data.policies, data.meta.username
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/renew-self {} X-Vault-Token: ... -> 200 auth.lease_duration
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/revoke-self X-Vault-Token: ... -> 204 (the logout)
        //   GET  /v1/auth/token/lookup-self  X-Vault-Token: ... -> 403 (a revoked token is gone)
        // The passwords are REDACTED[alice] and REDACTED[alice-wrong-password]
        // on the tape; a port sends "alice-pass" and "not-the-password". Take
        // the client token from the replayed login response, as a client would.
        spec.it("logs in with userpass and ends the session") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("logs_in_with_userpass_and_ends_the_session", [], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "no token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "permission denied", "permission denied")

            st, b = anonymous("POST", "auth/userpass/login/alice", "{\"password\":\"not-the-password\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 500, "a wrong password is refused (Vault 1.13 answers 500, not 400/401): ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "invalid username or password", "invalid username or password")

            st, b = anonymous("POST", "auth/userpass/login/alice", "{\"password\":\"${ALICE_PASSWORD}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the right password logs in: ${b}")
            client_token = jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(client_token) > 0, "a client token")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"policies\":[\"default\",\"tcae-admin\"]", "alice's policies")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"lease_duration\":2764800", "the default 32 days")

            st, b = vault_as(client_token, "GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "lookup-self with the client token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.display_name"), "userpass-alice", "who it is")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.meta.username"), "alice", "the user name")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.path"), "auth/userpass/login/alice", "how it was made")

            st, b = vault_as(client_token, "POST", "auth/token/renew-self", "{}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "renew-self: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"renewable\":true", "renewable")

            st, b = vault_as(client_token, "POST", "auth/token/revoke-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "revoke-self logs out: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as(client_token, "GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "a revoked token is refused: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: the approle login. Starts logged in (alice's token), then:
        //   POST   /v1/sys/auth/tcae-approle {"type":"approle"} -> 204
        //   POST   /v1/auth/tcae-approle/role/r1 {"token_policies":["default"],"token_ttl":"1h"} -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/auth/tcae-approle/role/r1/role-id -> 200 data.role_id ({{uuid-N}})
        //   POST   /v1/auth/tcae-approle/role/r1/secret-id (no body) -> 200 data.secret_id ({{uuid-N}})
        //   POST   /v1/auth/tcae-approle/login {"role_id":..,"secret_id":"not-the-secret-id"} (no token) -> 500
        //          {"errors":["invalid secret id"]}
        //   POST   /v1/auth/tcae-approle/login {"role_id":..,"secret_id":..} (no token) -> 200,
        //          auth.client_token, auth.metadata.role_name "r1", auth.policies ["default"],
        //          auth.lease_duration 3600
        //   GET    /v1/auth/token/lookup-self with that token -> 200, data.display_name "tcae-approle"
        //   DELETE /v1/sys/auth/tcae-approle -> 204 (the method is removed with its roles and tokens)
        //   POST   /v1/auth/tcae-approle/login {..} (no token) -> 403 permission denied (the method is gone)
        // The role id and secret id are uuids, normalized: send what the
        // responses gave. The secret id literal is not a uuid, so it stays as
        // written.
        spec.it("logs in with an approle") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("logs_in_with_an_approle", ["sys/auth/tcae-approle"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "sys/auth/tcae-approle", "{\"type\":\"approle\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "enable approle: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/tcae-approle/role/r1", "{\"token_policies\":[\"default\"],\"token_ttl\":\"1h\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "create the role: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "auth/tcae-approle/role/r1/role-id", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "role id: ${b}")
            role_id = jstr(b, "data.role_id")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(role_id) > 0, "a role id")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/tcae-approle/role/r1/secret-id", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "secret id: ${b}")
            secret_id = jstr(b, "data.secret_id")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(secret_id) > 0, "a secret id")

            st, b = anonymous("POST", "auth/tcae-approle/login", "{\"role_id\":\"${role_id}\",\"secret_id\":\"not-the-secret-id\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 500, "a wrong secret id (Vault 1.13 answers 500): ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "invalid secret id", "invalid secret id")
            st, b = anonymous("POST", "auth/tcae-approle/login", "{\"role_id\":\"${role_id}\",\"secret_id\":\"${secret_id}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the right ids log in: ${b}")
            approle_token = jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(approle_token) > 0, "a client token")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "auth.metadata.role_name"), "r1", "the role")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"policies\":[\"default\"]", "the role's policies")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"lease_duration\":3600", "the role's ttl")
            st, b = vault_as(approle_token, "GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "lookup-self: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.display_name"), "tcae-approle", "who it is (the mount's name)")

            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "sys/auth/tcae-approle", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "disable approle: ${b}")
            st, b = anonymous("POST", "auth/tcae-approle/login", "{\"role_id\":\"${role_id}\",\"secret_id\":\"${secret_id}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "the method is gone, so the route is unauthenticated: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: nobody, or somebody wrong. The first four send no token.
        //   GET /v1/sys/health                 -> 200 (public)
        //   GET /v1/secret/data/tcae/private   -> 403 {"errors":["permission denied"]}
        //   GET /v1/sys/mounts                 -> 403
        //   PUT /v1/secret/data/tcae/private {"data":{"a":"b"}} -> 403
        //   GET /v1/secret/data/tcae/private  X-Vault-Token: not-a-token -> 403 (same body;
        //     the tape's header is X_VAULT_TOKEN_1 and replay matches on presence,
        //     so replay cannot tell this from a good token, only Vault could)
        spec.it("refuses a client without a valid token") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("refuses_a_client_without_a_valid_token", [], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "sys/health", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "health needs no token: ${b}")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "secret/data/tcae/private", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "reading needs a token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"errors\":[\"permission denied\"]}\n", "permission denied")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "sys/mounts", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "listing mounts needs a token: ${b}")
            st, b = anonymous("PUT", "secret/data/tcae/private", "{\"data\":{\"a\":\"b\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "writing needs a token: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as("not-a-token", "GET", "secret/data/tcae/private", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "a made-up token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"errors\":[\"permission denied\"]}\n", "permission denied")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- sys -------------------------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: the public status endpoints, no token on any of them.
        //   GET /v1/sys/health -> 200 {"initialized":true,"sealed":false,"standby":false,..,
        //        "version":"1.13.0","cluster_name":"vault-cluster-0","cluster_id":"{{uuid-1}}"}
        //   GET /v1/sys/health?activecode=202 -> 202, same body (the status for "active" is
        //        chosen by the client: load balancers use this)
        //   GET /v1/sys/health?standbyok=true&perfstandbyok=true -> 200
        //   GET /v1/sys/seal-status -> 200 {"type":"shamir","initialized":true,"sealed":false,
        //        "t":1,"n":1,"progress":0,..,"storage_type":"inmem"}
        //   GET /v1/sys/leader -> 200 {"ha_enabled":false,..,"leader_address":""}
        //   GET /v1/sys/init   -> 200 {"initialized":true}
        spec.it("reports health, seal status, leader and init without a token") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_health_seal_status_leader_and_init", [], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "sys/health", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "health: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"initialized\":true", "initialized")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"sealed\":false", "unsealed")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"standby\":false", "active")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"version\":\"1.13.0\"", "version")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "sys/health?activecode=202", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 202, "the status for an active node is the client's choice: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"initialized\":true", "the same body")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "sys/health?standbyok=true&perfstandbyok=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "standbyok: ${b}")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "sys/seal-status", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "seal-status: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"type\":\"shamir\"", "shamir")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"sealed\":false", "unsealed")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"t\":1,\"n\":1", "one key of one")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "sys/leader", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "leader: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"ha_enabled\":false", "no HA")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "sys/init", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "init: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"initialized\":true}\n", "initialized")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: mounts, in tcae-kv (a KV v1 engine). Read through
        // sys/internal/ui/mounts, not sys/mounts (see "Awkward points").
        //   GET    /v1/sys/internal/ui/mounts -> 200 data.secret has "secret/" and "sys/"...,
        //          data.auth has "token/" and "userpass/"
        //   POST   /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-mount {"type":"kv","description":"a first mount","options":{"version":"1"}} -> 204
        //   POST   /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-mount (the same) -> 400 {"errors":["path is already in use at tcae-mount/"]}
        //   GET    /v1/sys/internal/ui/mounts/tcae-mount -> 200 data.type "kv", data.description,
        //          data.options.version "1", data.path "tcae-mount/", data.accessor {{mount-accessor-N}}
        //   POST   /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-mount/tune {"description":"a tuned mount","default_lease_ttl":"2h"} -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/sys/internal/ui/mounts/tcae-mount -> the new description, config.default_lease_ttl 7200
        //   DELETE /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-mount -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/tcae-mount/x -> 404 {"errors":["no handler for route ..."]}
        spec.it("mounts, tunes and unmounts a secrets engine") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("mounts_tunes_and_unmounts_a_secrets_engine", ["sys/mounts/tcae-mount"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("GET", "sys/internal/ui/mounts", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the mounts: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"secret/\":{", "the dev server's KV mount")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"userpass/\":{", "the userpass auth method the setup enabled")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"token/\":{", "the token auth method")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "sys/mounts/tcae-mount", "{\"type\":\"kv\",\"description\":\"a first mount\",\"options\":{\"version\":\"1\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "mount: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "sys/mounts/tcae-mount", "{\"type\":\"kv\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "mounting twice: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "path is already in use at tcae-mount/", "already in use")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "sys/internal/ui/mounts/tcae-mount", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read the mount: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.type"), "kv", "its type")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.description"), "a first mount", "its description")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.options.version"), "1", "KV version 1")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.path"), "tcae-mount/", "its path")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "sys/mounts/tcae-mount/tune", "{\"description\":\"a tuned mount\",\"default_lease_ttl\":\"2h\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "tune: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "sys/internal/ui/mounts/tcae-mount", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.description"), "a tuned mount", "the new description: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"default_lease_ttl\":7200", "the new default lease ttl")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "sys/mounts/tcae-mount", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "unmount: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "tcae-mount/x", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "nothing is mounted there now: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "no handler for route", "no handler for the route")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: ACL policies, named tcae-test.
        //   PUT    /v1/sys/policies/acl/tcae-test {"policy":"path \"secret/data/tcae/*\" {...}"} -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/sys/policies/acl/tcae-test -> 200 data.name, data.policy (the text, with \n)
        //   PUT    /v1/sys/policies/acl/tcae-test (a second policy text) -> 204 (an update)
        //   GET    /v1/sys/policies/acl?list=true -> 200 data.keys ["default","tcae-admin","tcae-reader","tcae-test","root"]
        //          (that order: Vault puts root last)
        //   POST   /v1/sys/capabilities-self {"paths":["secret/data/tcae/x","sys/mounts"]}
        //          -> 200 data["secret/data/tcae/x"] the alice's capabilities (sudo included)
        //   DELETE /v1/sys/policies/acl/tcae-test -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/sys/policies/acl/tcae-test -> 404 {"errors":[]}
        spec.it("writes, reads, lists and deletes an ACL policy") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("writes_reads_lists_and_deletes_an_acl_policy", ["sys/policies/acl/tcae-test"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            p1 = "path 'secret/data/tcae/*' {\n  capabilities = ['read']\n}"
            p2 = "path 'secret/data/tcae/*' {\n  capabilities = ['read', 'list']\n}"
            st, b = vault_("PUT", "sys/policies/acl/tcae-test", "{\"policy\":\"${hcl(p1)}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "write: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "sys/policies/acl/tcae-test", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.name"), "tcae-test", "its name")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.policy"), string.replace_all(p1, "'", "\""), "the text as written")
            st, b = vault_("PUT", "sys/policies/acl/tcae-test", "{\"policy\":\"${hcl(p2)}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "update: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "sys/policies/acl?list=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"keys\":[\"default\",\"tcae-admin\",\"tcae-reader\",\"tcae-test\",\"root\"]", "the policies, root last")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "sys/capabilities-self", "{\"paths\":[\"secret/data/tcae/x\",\"sys/mounts\"]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "capabilities: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"sudo\"", "alice may sudo")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "sys/policies/acl/tcae-test", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "delete: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "sys/policies/acl/tcae-test", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "gone: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"errors\":[]}\n", "an empty error list")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: tcae-reader may read and list under secret/*/tcae/ and
        // nothing else. Alice (admin token, X_VAULT_TOKEN_1) writes; bob (the
        // reader, a second token) reads. Each bob refusal is
        // {"errors":["1 error occurred:\n\t* permission denied\n\n"]} (a
        // different body from the "permission denied" a missing token gets).
        //   alice POST /v1/secret/data/tcae/shared {"data":{"colour":"green"}} -> 200
        //   bob   GET  /v1/secret/data/tcae/shared -> 200, the secret
        //   bob   GET  /v1/secret/metadata/tcae?list=true -> 200 keys ["shared"]
        //   bob   POST /v1/secret/data/tcae/shared {"data":{"colour":"red"}} -> 403
        //   bob   DELETE /v1/secret/data/tcae/shared -> 403
        //   bob   GET  /v1/secret/data/other/x -> 403
        //   bob   GET  /v1/sys/policies/acl/tcae-admin -> 403
        //   bob   POST /v1/sys/capabilities-self {"paths":["secret/data/tcae/shared","secret/data/other/x"]}
        //         -> 200, ["read"] and ["deny"]
        //   alice DELETE /v1/secret/metadata/tcae/shared -> 204
        // (Replay matches the token header on presence, so it cannot check
        // that bob's token, not alice's, was sent: the assertions on the
        // responses are what show it.)
        spec.it("enforces a read-only policy") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("enforces_a_read_only_policy", ["secret/metadata/tcae/shared"], 1)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/shared", "{\"data\":{\"colour\":\"green\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "alice writes: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as(bob_tok, "GET", "secret/data/tcae/shared", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "bob reads: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(kv_field(b, "colour"), "green", "the secret")
            st, b = vault_as(bob_tok, "GET", "secret/metadata/tcae?list=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "bob lists: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"keys\":[\"shared\"]", "the one secret")
            st, b = vault_as(bob_tok, "POST", "secret/data/tcae/shared", "{\"data\":{\"colour\":\"red\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "bob cannot write: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "permission denied", "permission denied")
            st, b = vault_as(bob_tok, "DELETE", "secret/data/tcae/shared", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "bob cannot delete: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as(bob_tok, "GET", "secret/data/other/x", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "bob cannot read elsewhere: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as(bob_tok, "GET", "sys/policies/acl/tcae-admin", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "bob cannot read policies: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as(bob_tok, "POST", "sys/capabilities-self", "{\"paths\":[\"secret/data/tcae/shared\",\"secret/data/other/x\"]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "bob's capabilities: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"secret/data/tcae/shared\":[\"read\"]", "read only")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"secret/data/other/x\":[\"deny\"]", "denied elsewhere")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "secret/metadata/tcae/shared", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "alice cleans up: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- KV v2 -----------------------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: versions of one secret, secret/tcae/versioned (the dev
        // server mounts KV v2 at secret/, so data is at secret/data/... and
        // metadata at secret/metadata/...).
        //   POST /v1/secret/data/tcae/versioned {"data":{"foo":"bar"}} -> 200 data.version 1
        //   POST /v1/secret/data/tcae/versioned {"data":{"foo":"bar2"},"options":{"cas":1}} -> 200 data.version 2
        //   POST /v1/secret/data/tcae/versioned {"data":{"foo":"bar3"},"options":{"cas":1}} -> 400
        //        {"errors":["check-and-set parameter did not match the current version"]}
        //   GET  /v1/secret/data/tcae/versioned -> 200 data.data.foo "bar2", data.metadata.version 2
        //   GET  /v1/secret/data/tcae/versioned?version=1 -> 200 data.data.foo "bar"
        //   GET  /v1/secret/metadata/tcae/versioned -> 200 data.current_version 2, data.versions "1" and "2"
        //   GET  /v1/secret/data/tcae/versioned?version=9 -> 404 {"errors":[]}
        //   DELETE /v1/secret/metadata/tcae/versioned -> 204 (all versions and metadata)
        //   GET  /v1/secret/data/tcae/versioned -> 404
        spec.it("writes, reads and versions a KV v2 secret") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("kv2_writes_reads_and_versions_a_secret", ["secret/metadata/tcae/versioned"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/versioned", "{\"data\":{\"foo\":\"bar\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "write: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"version\":1", "version 1")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/versioned", "{\"data\":{\"foo\":\"bar2\"},\"options\":{\"cas\":1}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "write with cas 1: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"version\":2", "version 2")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/versioned", "{\"data\":{\"foo\":\"bar3\"},\"options\":{\"cas\":1}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a stale cas: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "check-and-set parameter did not match the current version", "the cas message")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/versioned", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(kv_field(b, "foo"), "bar2", "the latest")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"version\":2", "version 2")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/versioned?version=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read version 1: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(kv_field(b, "foo"), "bar", "the first")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/metadata/tcae/versioned", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "metadata: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"current_version\":2", "current version")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"versions\":{\"1\":{", "version 1 listed")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"2\":{", "version 2 listed")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/versioned?version=9", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a version that does not exist: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "secret/metadata/tcae/versioned", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "delete everything: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/versioned", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "gone: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: soft delete, undelete and destroy, secret/tcae/lifecycle
        // (two versions written first: {"data":{"n":"one"}} and {"data":{"n":"two"}}).
        //   DELETE /v1/secret/data/tcae/lifecycle -> 204 (soft-deletes the latest version)
        //   GET    /v1/secret/data/tcae/lifecycle -> 404 with a body: data.data null,
        //          data.metadata.deletion_time set (collapsed), destroyed false
        //   POST   /v1/secret/undelete/tcae/lifecycle {"versions":[2]} -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/secret/data/tcae/lifecycle -> 200 "two" again
        //   POST   /v1/secret/delete/tcae/lifecycle {"versions":[1,2]} -> 204
        //   POST   /v1/secret/destroy/tcae/lifecycle {"versions":[1]} -> 204 (for good)
        //   GET    /v1/secret/data/tcae/lifecycle?version=1 -> 404, data.metadata.destroyed true
        //   POST   /v1/secret/undelete/tcae/lifecycle {"versions":[1,2]} -> 204, but only 2 comes back:
        //   GET    ...?version=1 -> still 404 destroyed; GET ...?version=2 -> 200 "two"
        //   DELETE /v1/secret/metadata/tcae/lifecycle -> 204
        spec.it("soft-deletes, undeletes and destroys KV v2 versions") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("kv2_soft_deletes_undeletes_and_destroys_versions", ["secret/metadata/tcae/lifecycle"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/lifecycle", "{\"data\":{\"n\":\"one\"}}")
            vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/lifecycle", "{\"data\":{\"n\":\"two\"}}")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "secret/data/tcae/lifecycle", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "soft delete: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/lifecycle", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a deleted version reads as 404: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"data\":null", "no data")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"destroyed\":false", "not destroyed")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"version\":2", "it is version 2 that was deleted")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/undelete/tcae/lifecycle", "{\"versions\":[2]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "undelete: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/lifecycle", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "back: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(kv_field(b, "n"), "two", "the value is intact")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/delete/tcae/lifecycle", "{\"versions\":[1,2]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "delete versions 1 and 2: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/destroy/tcae/lifecycle", "{\"versions\":[1]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "destroy version 1: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/lifecycle?version=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a destroyed version: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"destroyed\":true", "destroyed")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/undelete/tcae/lifecycle", "{\"versions\":[1,2]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "undelete 1 and 2: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/lifecycle?version=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "version 1 stays destroyed: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/lifecycle?version=2", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "version 2 is back: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "secret/metadata/tcae/lifecycle", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "delete everything: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: listing, metadata and patching, under secret/tcae/tree/.
        //   POST /v1/secret/data/tcae/tree/a {"data":{"k":"1"}} -> 200 (also tree/b and tree/sub/c)
        //   GET  /v1/secret/metadata/tcae/tree?list=true -> 200 data.keys ["a","b","sub/"] (folders end in /)
        //   GET  /v1/secret/metadata/tcae/tree/sub?list=true -> 200 keys ["c"]
        //   GET  /v1/secret/metadata/tcae/nothing?list=true -> 404 {"errors":[]}
        //   POST /v1/secret/metadata/tcae/tree/a {"max_versions":2,"custom_metadata":{"owner":"tcae"}} -> 204
        //   POST /v1/secret/data/tcae/tree/a {"data":{"k":"2"}} and {"data":{"k":"3"}} -> 200 versions 2 and 3
        //   GET  /v1/secret/metadata/tcae/tree/a -> 200 max_versions 2, oldest_version 2,
        //        custom_metadata {"owner":"tcae"}, versions "2" and "3" only (1 was pruned)
        //   GET  /v1/secret/data/tcae/tree/a?version=1 -> 404
        //   PATCH /v1/secret/data/tcae/tree/a {"data":{"extra":"y"}} Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json
        //        -> 200 version 4; GET shows both k "3" and extra "y"
        //   PATCH /v1/secret/data/tcae/tree/nothing (same) -> 404
        //   DELETE /v1/secret/metadata/tcae/tree/{a,b,sub/c} -> 204 each
        spec.it("lists, annotates and patches KV v2 secrets") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("kv2_lists_annotates_and_patches_secrets", ["secret/metadata/tcae/tree/a", "secret/metadata/tcae/tree/b", "secret/metadata/tcae/tree/sub/c"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/tree/a", "{\"data\":{\"k\":\"1\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "write a: ${b}")
            vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/tree/b", "{\"data\":{\"k\":\"1\"}}")
            vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/tree/sub/c", "{\"data\":{\"k\":\"1\"}}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/metadata/tcae/tree?list=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"keys\":[\"a\",\"b\",\"sub/\"]", "keys, folders ending in a slash")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/metadata/tcae/tree/sub?list=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list the folder: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"keys\":[\"c\"]", "its one secret")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/metadata/tcae/nothing?list=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "list where nothing is: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/metadata/tcae/tree/a", "{\"max_versions\":2,\"custom_metadata\":{\"owner\":\"tcae\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "metadata: ${b}")
            vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/tree/a", "{\"data\":{\"k\":\"2\"}}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/tree/a", "{\"data\":{\"k\":\"3\"}}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"version\":3", "version 3")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/metadata/tcae/tree/a", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read the metadata: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"max_versions\":2", "max_versions")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"oldest_version\":2", "version 1 was pruned")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"custom_metadata\":{\"owner\":\"tcae\"}", "custom metadata")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/tree/a?version=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a pruned version: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_with(tok, "PATCH", "secret/data/tcae/tree/a", "application/merge-patch+json", [], "{\"data\":{\"extra\":\"y\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "patch: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"version\":4", "a new version")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/tree/a", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(kv_field(b, "k"), "3", "the old field is kept: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(kv_field(b, "extra"), "y", "the new field is added")
            st, b = vault_with(tok, "PATCH", "secret/data/tcae/tree/nothing", "application/merge-patch+json", [], "{\"data\":{\"extra\":\"y\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "patching what is not there: ${b}")
            vault_("DELETE", "secret/metadata/tcae/tree/a", "")
            vault_("DELETE", "secret/metadata/tcae/tree/b", "")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "secret/metadata/tcae/tree/sub/c", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "clean up: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- KV v1, the cubbyhole and wrapping -------------------------------

        // PORTING: a KV v1 engine mounted at tcae-kv1 (no versions: the
        // path is the secret's path, the body is its data).
        //   POST   /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-kv1 {"type":"kv","options":{"version":"1"}} -> 204
        //   POST   /v1/tcae-kv1/app {"user":"u","pass":"p"} -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/tcae-kv1/app -> 200 data {"pass":"p","user":"u"}, lease_duration 2764800
        //   POST   /v1/tcae-kv1/app/db {"host":"h"} -> 204 ; GET /v1/tcae-kv1?list=true -> keys ["app","app/"]
        //   POST   /v1/tcae-kv1/app {"user":"u2"} -> 204 (replaces the whole secret)
        //   GET    /v1/tcae-kv1/app -> data {"user":"u2"}
        //   DELETE /v1/tcae-kv1/app -> 204 ; GET -> 404 {"errors":[]}
        //   DELETE /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-kv1 -> 204
        spec.it("stores and lists KV v1 secrets") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("kv1_stores_replaces_lists_and_deletes_secrets", ["sys/mounts/tcae-kv1"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "sys/mounts/tcae-kv1", "{\"type\":\"kv\",\"options\":{\"version\":\"1\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "mount: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-kv1/app", "{\"user\":\"u\",\"pass\":\"p\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "write: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "tcae-kv1/app", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"data\":{\"pass\":\"p\",\"user\":\"u\"}", "the data, flat")
            vault_("POST", "tcae-kv1/app/db", "{\"host\":\"h\"}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "tcae-kv1?list=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"keys\":[\"app\",\"app/\"]", "a secret and a folder of the same name")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-kv1/app", "{\"user\":\"u2\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "replace: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "tcae-kv1/app", "")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"data\":{\"user\":\"u2\"}", "replaced, not merged")
            vault_("DELETE", "tcae-kv1/app/db", "")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "tcae-kv1/app", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "delete: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "tcae-kv1/app", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "gone: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "sys/mounts/tcae-kv1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "unmount: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: a response is wrapped when the request carries
        // X-Vault-Wrap-TTL; the wrapping token unwraps once.
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/create {"policies":["default"],"ttl":"1h"} X-Vault-Wrap-TTL: 60
        //        -> 200 with data null and wrap_info {token ({{token-N}} or X_VAULT_TOKEN_N),
        //        ttl 60, creation_path "auth/token/create", wrapped_accessor}; no auth block
        //   POST /v1/sys/wrapping/lookup {"token":<the wrapping token>} (no X-Vault-Token) -> 200
        //        data.creation_path, data.creation_ttl 60
        //   POST /v1/sys/wrapping/unwrap (no body) X-Vault-Token: <the wrapping token> -> 200,
        //        auth.client_token, the token that was wrapped, auth.policies ["default"]
        //   POST /v1/sys/wrapping/unwrap X-Vault-Token: <the wrapping token> -> 400
        //        {"errors":["wrapping token is not valid or does not exist"]} (it was single use)
        //   GET  /v1/auth/token/lookup-self X-Vault-Token: <the unwrapped token> -> 200
        spec.it("wraps a response and unwraps it once") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("wraps_a_response_and_unwraps_it_once", [], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_with(tok, "POST", "auth/token/create", "application/json", ["X-Vault-Wrap-TTL: 60"], "{\"policies\":[\"default\"],\"ttl\":\"1h\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create, wrapped: ${b}")
            wrap = jstr(b, "wrap_info.token")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(wrap) > 0, "a wrapping token")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"data\":null", "the response itself is not here")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "wrap_info.creation_path"), "auth/token/create", "what was wrapped")
            st, b = anonymous("POST", "sys/wrapping/lookup", "{\"token\":\"${wrap}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "lookup the wrapping token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.creation_path"), "auth/token/create", "its creation path")
            st, b = vault_as(wrap, "POST", "sys/wrapping/unwrap", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "unwrap: ${b}")
            unwrapped = jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(unwrapped) > 0, "the wrapped token")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"policies\":[\"default\"]", "its policies")
            st, b = vault_as(wrap, "POST", "sys/wrapping/unwrap", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "unwrapping twice: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "wrapping token is not valid or does not exist", "single use")
            st, b = vault_as(unwrapped, "GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the unwrapped token works: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: the cubbyhole is private to each token.
        //   POST /v1/cubbyhole/tcae {"a":"b"} (alice's token) -> 204
        //   GET  /v1/cubbyhole/tcae (alice's token) -> 200 data {"a":"b"}
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/create {"policies":["tcae-admin"],"ttl":"1h"} -> 200, auth.client_token (a second token)
        //   GET  /v1/cubbyhole/tcae (the second token) -> 404 {"errors":[]}: its own, empty, cubbyhole
        //   DELETE /v1/cubbyhole/tcae (alice's token) -> 204
        spec.it("keeps the cubbyhole private to each token") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("keeps_the_cubbyhole_private_to_each_token", [], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "cubbyhole/tcae", "{\"a\":\"b\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "write: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "cubbyhole/tcae", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"data\":{\"a\":\"b\"}", "the data")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/create", "{\"policies\":[\"tcae-admin\"],\"ttl\":\"1h\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "a second token: ${b}")
            other = jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
            st, b = vault_as(other, "GET", "cubbyhole/tcae", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "another token's cubbyhole is empty: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "cubbyhole/tcae", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "clean up: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- transit -----------------------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: a key's life, in the engine mounted at tcae-transit.
        //   POST   /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-transit {"type":"transit"} -> 204
        //   POST   /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k1 {"type":"aes256-gcm96"} -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k1 -> 200 data.type, data.latest_version 1, data.keys {"1":<time>},
        //          data.deletion_allowed false, data.supports_encryption true
        //   POST   /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k1/rotate -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k1 -> latest_version 2, keys "1" and "2"
        //   POST   /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k1/config {"min_decryption_version":2,"deletion_allowed":true} -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k1 -> min_decryption_version 2, keys now only "2"
        //   POST   /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k2 {"type":"ed25519"} -> 204
        //   GET    /v1/tcae-transit/keys?list=true -> keys ["k1","k2"]
        //   DELETE /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k1 -> 204 (deletion_allowed was set)
        //   DELETE /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k2 -> 400 {"errors":["key is marked as not deletable..."]}
        //   GET    /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k1 -> 404 {"errors":[]}
        //   DELETE /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-transit -> 204
        spec.it("creates, rotates, configures and deletes a transit key") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("transit_creates_rotates_configures_and_deletes_a_key", ["sys/mounts/tcae-transit"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "sys/mounts/tcae-transit", "{\"type\":\"transit\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "mount: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/keys/k1", "{\"type\":\"aes256-gcm96\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "create: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "tcae-transit/keys/k1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.type"), "aes256-gcm96", "its type")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"latest_version\":1", "version 1")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"deletion_allowed\":false", "not deletable yet")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"supports_encryption\":true", "encrypts")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/keys/k1/rotate", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "rotate: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "tcae-transit/keys/k1", "")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"latest_version\":2", "version 2")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"keys\":{\"1\":", "key version 1 kept")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/keys/k1/config", "{\"min_decryption_version\":2,\"deletion_allowed\":true}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "config: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "tcae-transit/keys/k1", "")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"min_decryption_version\":2", "min_decryption_version")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"deletion_allowed\":true", "deletable")
            spec.assert_true(string.contains(b, "\"keys\":{\"1\":") == 0, "key version 1 no longer offered")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/keys/k2", "{\"type\":\"ed25519\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "create k2: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "tcae-transit/keys?list=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"keys\":[\"k1\",\"k2\"]", "both keys")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "tcae-transit/keys/k1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "delete k1: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "tcae-transit/keys/k2", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "k2 is not deletable: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "tcae-transit/keys/k1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "k1 is gone: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "sys/mounts/tcae-transit", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "unmount: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: encryption as a service, key tcae-transit/keys/k1. The
        // plaintext is base64 ("aGVsbG8gdHJhbnNpdA==" is "hello transit").
        //   POST /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-transit {"type":"transit"} -> 204 ; POST /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k1 {"type":"aes256-gcm96"} -> 204
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/encrypt/k1 {"plaintext":"aGVsbG8gdHJhbnNpdA=="} -> 200
        //        data.ciphertext {{blob-1}} ("vault:v1:..."), data.key_version 1
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/decrypt/k1 {"ciphertext":<it>} -> 200 data.plaintext "aGVsbG8gdHJhbnNpdA=="
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/keys/k1/rotate -> 204
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/rewrap/k1 {"ciphertext":<it>} -> 200 data.ciphertext {{blob-2}}, key_version 2
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/decrypt/k1 {"ciphertext":<the rewrapped>} -> the same plaintext
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/decrypt/k1 {"ciphertext":<the old v1 one>} -> 200 too (v1 is still allowed)
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/encrypt/k1 {"batch_input":[{"plaintext":"YQ=="},{"plaintext":"Yg=="}]} -> 200
        //        data.batch_results, two ciphertexts
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/decrypt/k1 {"ciphertext":"not-a-ciphertext"} -> 400
        //        {"errors":["invalid ciphertext: no prefix"]}
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/keys/nosuchkey/rotate -> 400 {"errors":["no existing key named nosuchkey could be found"]}
        //        (encrypt, unlike rotate, CREATES a missing key on first use, so it is not an error case)
        //   DELETE /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-transit -> 204
        spec.it("encrypts, decrypts and rewraps with transit") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("transit_encrypts_decrypts_and_rewraps", ["sys/mounts/tcae-transit"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            vault_("POST", "sys/mounts/tcae-transit", "{\"type\":\"transit\"}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/keys/k1", "{\"type\":\"aes256-gcm96\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "create the key: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/encrypt/k1", "{\"plaintext\":\"aGVsbG8gdHJhbnNpdA==\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "encrypt: ${b}")
            ct1 = jstr(b, "data.ciphertext")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(ct1) > 0, "a ciphertext")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"key_version\":1", "key version 1")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/decrypt/k1", "{\"ciphertext\":\"${ct1}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "decrypt: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.plaintext"), "aGVsbG8gdHJhbnNpdA==", "the plaintext comes back")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/keys/k1/rotate", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "rotate: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/rewrap/k1", "{\"ciphertext\":\"${ct1}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "rewrap: ${b}")
            ct2 = jstr(b, "data.ciphertext")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(ct2) > 0, "a new ciphertext")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"key_version\":2", "now under key version 2")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/decrypt/k1", "{\"ciphertext\":\"${ct2}\"}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.plaintext"), "aGVsbG8gdHJhbnNpdA==", "the rewrapped ciphertext decrypts to the same: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/decrypt/k1", "{\"ciphertext\":\"${ct1}\"}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.plaintext"), "aGVsbG8gdHJhbnNpdA==", "the old one still does: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/encrypt/k1", "{\"batch_input\":[{\"plaintext\":\"YQ==\"},{\"plaintext\":\"Yg==\"}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "batch encrypt: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(jstr(b, "data.batch_results.1.ciphertext")) > 0, "two results")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/decrypt/k1", "{\"ciphertext\":\"not-a-ciphertext\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a ciphertext that is not one: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "invalid ciphertext", "invalid ciphertext")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/keys/nosuchkey/rotate", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "rotating a key that does not exist: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "sys/mounts/tcae-transit", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "unmount: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: signing, verifying, hashing and HMAC, key ed25519 (k2) and
        // aes256-gcm96 (k1) in tcae-transit. Inputs are base64 ("aGVsbG8=" is "hello").
        //   POST /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-transit {"type":"transit"}; POST .../keys/k2 {"type":"ed25519"}; POST .../keys/k1 {"type":"aes256-gcm96"}
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/sign/k2 {"input":"aGVsbG8="} -> 200 data.signature {{blob-1}}, key_version 1
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/verify/k2 {"input":"aGVsbG8=","signature":<it>} -> 200 data.valid true
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/verify/k2 {"input":"d29ybGQ=","signature":<it>} -> 200 data.valid false ("world")
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/hash/sha2-256 {"input":"aGVsbG8="} -> 200 data.sum, deterministic:
        //        2cf24dba5fb0a30e26e83b2ac5b9e29e1b161e5c1fa7425e73043362938b9824 (the same everywhere)
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/hmac/k1 {"input":"aGVsbG8="} -> 200 data.hmac {{blob-2}}
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/verify/k1 {"input":"aGVsbG8=","hmac":<it>} -> 200 data.valid true
        //   POST /v1/tcae-transit/sign/k1 {"input":"aGVsbG8="} -> 400 (an aes key cannot sign)
        //   DELETE /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-transit -> 204
        spec.it("signs, verifies, hashes and HMACs with transit") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("transit_signs_verifies_hashes_and_hmacs", ["sys/mounts/tcae-transit"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            vault_("POST", "sys/mounts/tcae-transit", "{\"type\":\"transit\"}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/keys/k2", "{\"type\":\"ed25519\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "create k2: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/keys/k1", "{\"type\":\"aes256-gcm96\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "create k1: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/sign/k2", "{\"input\":\"aGVsbG8=\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "sign: ${b}")
            sig = jstr(b, "data.signature")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(sig) > 0, "a signature")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/verify/k2", "{\"input\":\"aGVsbG8=\",\"signature\":\"${sig}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "verify: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"valid\":true", "valid")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/verify/k2", "{\"input\":\"d29ybGQ=\",\"signature\":\"${sig}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "verify other input: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"valid\":false", "not valid for other input")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/hash/sha2-256", "{\"input\":\"aGVsbG8=\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "hash: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.sum"), "2cf24dba5fb0a30e26e83b2ac5b9e29e1b161e5c1fa7425e73043362938b9824", "sha-256 of hello")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/hmac/k1", "{\"input\":\"aGVsbG8=\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "hmac: ${b}")
            mac = jstr(b, "data.hmac")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(mac) > 0, "an hmac")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/verify/k1", "{\"input\":\"aGVsbG8=\",\"hmac\":\"${mac}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "verify hmac: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"valid\":true", "valid hmac")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "tcae-transit/sign/k1", "{\"input\":\"aGVsbG8=\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "an aes key cannot sign: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("DELETE", "sys/mounts/tcae-transit", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "unmount: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- tokens ------------------------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: a child token's life.
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/create {"policies":["default"],"ttl":"1h","display_name":"child","renewable":true}
        //        -> 200 auth.client_token, auth.accessor ({{accessor-N}}), auth.policies ["default"],
        //        auth.lease_duration 3600, auth.orphan false
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/lookup {"token":<it>} -> 200 data.display_name "token-child", data.creation_ttl 3600,
        //        data.ttl 3600 (it counts down on a real server: collapsed on the tape), data.policies ["default"]
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/lookup-accessor {"accessor":<its accessor>} -> 200, the same data (without the id)
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/renew {"token":<it>,"increment":"2h"} -> 200 auth.lease_duration 7200
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/revoke {"token":<it>} -> 204
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/lookup {"token":<it>} -> 403 {"errors":["bad token"]}
        // Create/lookup/renew/revoke here are all done with alice's token in
        // the header; the child's own token is only ever in a body.
        spec.it("creates, looks up, renews and revokes a child token") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("creates_looks_up_renews_and_revokes_a_child_token", [], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/create", "{\"policies\":[\"default\"],\"ttl\":\"1h\",\"display_name\":\"child\",\"renewable\":true}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create: ${b}")
            child = jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
            acc = jstr(b, "auth.accessor")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(child) > 0, "a client token")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(acc) > 0, "an accessor")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"policies\":[\"default\"]", "policies")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"lease_duration\":3600", "an hour")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"orphan\":false", "a child of alice's token")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/lookup", "{\"token\":\"${child}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "lookup: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.display_name"), "token-child", "display name")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"creation_ttl\":3600", "creation_ttl")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/lookup-accessor", "{\"accessor\":\"${acc}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "lookup by accessor: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "data.display_name"), "token-child", "the same token")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/renew", "{\"token\":\"${child}\",\"increment\":\"2h\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "renew: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"lease_duration\":7200", "two hours")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/revoke", "{\"token\":\"${child}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "revoke: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/lookup", "{\"token\":\"${child}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "a revoked token is gone: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: a use limit, and revoking by accessor.
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/create {"policies":["default"],"num_uses":2,"ttl":"1h"} -> 200 auth.num_uses 2
        //   GET  /v1/auth/token/lookup-self X-Vault-Token: <it> -> 200 (first use)
        //   GET  /v1/auth/token/lookup-self X-Vault-Token: <it> -> 200 (second and last use)
        //   GET  /v1/auth/token/lookup-self X-Vault-Token: <it> -> 403 (spent)
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/create {"policies":["default"],"ttl":"1h"} -> 200, a second token, with accessor
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/revoke-accessor {"accessor":<its accessor>} -> 204
        //   GET  /v1/auth/token/lookup-self X-Vault-Token: <the second> -> 403
        spec.it("limits a token's uses and revokes one by accessor") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("limits_a_tokens_uses_and_revokes_one_by_accessor", [], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/create", "{\"policies\":[\"default\"],\"num_uses\":2,\"ttl\":\"1h\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create: ${b}")
            limited = jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"num_uses\":2", "two uses")
            st, b = vault_as(limited, "GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "first use: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as(limited, "GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "second use: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as(limited, "GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "spent: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/create", "{\"policies\":[\"default\"],\"ttl\":\"1h\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create another: ${b}")
            second = jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
            acc = jstr(b, "auth.accessor")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/revoke-accessor", "{\"accessor\":\"${acc}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "revoke by accessor: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as(second, "GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "revoked: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: revoking a token revokes the tokens it made.
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/create {"policies":["tcae-admin"],"ttl":"1h"} -> the parent
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/create {"policies":["default"],"ttl":"1h"} X-Vault-Token: <parent> -> the child
        //        (auth.orphan false); and one more with {"policies":["default"],"ttl":"1h","no_parent":true} -> an orphan
        //   POST /v1/auth/token/revoke {"token":<parent>} -> 204
        //   GET  /v1/auth/token/lookup-self X-Vault-Token: <child> -> 403 (gone with the parent)
        //   GET  /v1/auth/token/lookup-self X-Vault-Token: <orphan> -> 200 (made by the parent, but no_parent)
        spec.it("revokes a token's children with it") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("revokes_a_tokens_children_with_it", [], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/create", "{\"policies\":[\"tcae-admin\"],\"ttl\":\"1h\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the parent: ${b}")
            parent = jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
            st, b = vault_as(parent, "POST", "auth/token/create", "{\"policies\":[\"default\"],\"ttl\":\"1h\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the child: ${b}")
            child = jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"orphan\":false", "not an orphan")
            st, b = vault_as(parent, "POST", "auth/token/create", "{\"policies\":[\"default\"],\"ttl\":\"1h\",\"no_parent\":true}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the orphan: ${b}")
            orphan = jstr(b, "auth.client_token")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"orphan\":true", "an orphan")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "auth/token/revoke", "{\"token\":\"${parent}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 204, "revoke the parent: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as(child, "GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "the child went with it: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_as(orphan, "GET", "auth/token/lookup-self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the orphan did not: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- errors --------------------------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: the representative error statuses, logged in as alice.
        //   POST /v1/secret/data/tcae/err {"data":"not an object"}   -> 400 (see the assertion)
        //   POST /v1/secret/data/tcae/err {} -> 400 {"errors":["no data provided"]}
        //   GET  /v1/secret/data/tcae/missing -> 404 {"errors":[]}
        //   GET  /v1/nosuch/x -> 404 {"errors":["no handler for route \"nosuch/x\". route entry not found."]}
        //   PATCH /v1/sys/health -> 405
        //   POST /v1/sys/mounts/tcae-bad {"type":"nosuchengine"} -> 400
        //   (403 is shown by the no-token and read-only cases; 429 and 503 need
        //   a standby or a sealed server, which a dev server never is)
        spec.it("answers the representative error statuses") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("answers_the_representative_error_statuses", ["sys/mounts/tcae-bad"], 0)
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/err", "{\"data\":\"not an object\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "data that is not an object: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "secret/data/tcae/err", "{}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "no data: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "no data provided", "no data provided")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "secret/data/tcae/missing", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a secret that is not there: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"errors\":[]}\n", "an empty error list")
            st, b = vault_("GET", "nosuch/x", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a path nothing is mounted at: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "no handler for route", "no handler for the route")
            st, b = vault_("PATCH", "sys/health", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 405, "PATCH is not offered: ${b}")
            st, b = vault_("POST", "sys/mounts/tcae-bad", "{\"type\":\"nosuchengine\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "an engine type that does not exist: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

    }

    if shared_container != null {
        e = tc.terminate(shared_container as *docker.Container)
        if e != "" { println("vault: removing the shared container: ${e}") }
    }
    return spec.run_summary(fw)
}
